kevin: Pushing an update to the Next.js samplekit that swaps from SWR to a small fetch-hook for embeddings. Noticed an auth refresh edge-case when the token expires mid-batch.

olivia: Ugh that sounds like the same thing I hit yesterday with SSR preview routes. Can you paste the snippet? :eyes:

kevin: Sure — current fetch wrapper in /lib/useEmbeddings.tsx:

```ts
async function fetchEmbeddings(texts: string[]) {
  const token = await auth.getAccessToken();
  const res = await fetch('/api/embeddings', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ inputs: texts })
  });
  if (res.status === 401) throw new Error('unauthorized');
  return res.json();
}
```

kevin: Problem: when multiple concurrent SWR revalidations happen, one request may get 401, refreshes token, but other inflight requests still fail and we don't retry.

olivia: We should centralize retry logic at the api route instead of each hook. That way server can do single refresh and replay.

maria: Is this SDK parity or just sample app wiring? If it's the SDK we should fix upstream. If not, doc update and small fix in samplekit.

sanjay: It's mostly sample wiring. Our hosted token refresh endpoint returns a new short-lived key for the client via /auth/refresh. If client code doesn't wait for refresh, you get race. One pattern: optimistic request queue in the browser that blocks on an ongoing refresh promise.

kevin: Implemented a minimal queue in samplekit. Code gist: 

```ts
let refreshPromise: Promise<void> | null = null;
async function withAuthRetry(fn) {
  try {
    return await fn();
  } catch (e) {
    if (e.message === 'unauthorized') {
      if (!refreshPromise) refreshPromise = auth.refresh();
      await refreshPromise;
      refreshPromise = null;
      return await fn(); // replay once
    }
    throw e;
  }
}
```

olivia: Nice. Can we add a unit test in the samplekit (jest) to simulate two concurrent calls where the first triggers refresh and second should succeed after replay?

kevin: Yep adding test now. Quick question — the sample /api/embeddings forwards to Redwood hosted API using server-side SDK call. We saw slightly different behavior between node SDK and browser fetch (CORS/token layering). Should we add a note about server vs client auth in onboarding docs?

maria: Please add a short section in Samplekit README explaining recommended pattern: prefer server-side call for embeddings when possible, or use the withAuthRetry helper for client usage. Also note token lifetime in console.

kevin: Done — pushed a tiny docs update and test. Running CI.

